1
00:00:00,103 --> 00:00:04,408
A Marsh Worth Protecting A marsh on the outskirts of town was

2
00:00:04,421 --> 00:00:08,934
once dismissed as useless land A developer wanted to drain it and

3
00:00:08,947 --> 00:00:15,447
construct a warehouse Local volunteers however argued that the apparent emptiness concealed

4
00:00:15,461 --> 00:00:20,605
a complex habitat A reed bed sheltered small animals while the shallow

5
00:00:20,618 --> 00:00:25,632
water offered a feeding ground for birds During an excursion we watched

6
00:00:25,645 --> 00:00:28,408
a woodpecker near a willow grove and a dove resting on a

7
00:00:28,421 --> 00:00:33,171
branch A snail moved across a damp leaf and a grasshopper clung

8
00:00:33,184 --> 00:00:37,487
to a stalk Our guide asked us not to trample the vegetation

9
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:42,355
or disturb a nest Even an organism that seemed trivial could contribute

10
00:00:42,368 --> 00:00:46,895
to the area's ecology The group prepared a proposal to reclaim a

11
00:00:46,908 --> 00:00:51,855
damaged section and restrict construction near the water It did not claim

12
00:00:51,868 --> 00:00:57,263
that preservation would solve every environmental problem Rather it showed how one

13
00:00:57,276 --> 00:01:03,237
practical intervention could protect a valuable locality Once a habitat is destroyed

14
00:01:03,474 --> 00:01:07,184
its restoration may demand far more time and money than its protection

15
00:01:07,197 --> 00:01:11,342
would have required Treating nature as an integral part of a city

16
00:01:11,355 --> 00:01:14,211
can therefore be both responsible and economical
